					<div class="font-bold text-slate-300 mb-1 flex items-center gap-1.5">
						<span>⚠️</span>
						<span class="lang-zh">信息论关键说明：特征之间的相关性陷阱</span>
						<span class="lang-en">Critical Information Theory Caveat: Feature Correlation</span>
					</div>
					<p>
						<span class="lang-zh">
							注：现实世界中的指纹特征绝非相互独立的硬币投掷。例如，时区为 <code>Asia/Shanghai</code> 的设备，其操作系统语言极大概率也是 <code>zh-CN</code>；macOS 系统几乎必定携带 Apple Silicon GPU 与特定的苹方（PingFang SC）字体。因此，各维度所拥有的信息熵<strong>绝不能简单做算术加法</strong>。追踪机构的算法（如决策树与贝叶斯网络）会自动根据互信息条件熵进行降维。经过严格折算后，主流现代桌面的有效联合熵仍在 25 至 30 比特区间，这依然足以让绝大多数访客在全球 85 亿人中成为“独一无二”。
						</span>
						<span class="lang-en">
							Note: Real-world attributes are never completely independent coin flips. A client in the <code>Asia/Shanghai</code> time zone has an overwhelmingly high probability of reporting <code>zh-CN</code> as its primary language; a macOS installation is strongly tied to Apple Silicon graphics and system fonts. Consequently, individual entropy figures <strong>cannot simply be summed arithmetically</strong>. Professional tracking pipelines leverage mutual conditional entropy to deflate duplicates. Even after this correlation discount, modern desktops typically retain 25 to 30 bits of joint entropy—more than enough to single out an individual among the 8.5 billion people on Earth.
						</span>
					</p>
