			<!-- 4. "WHY THIS WORKS" ORIGINAL EXPLAINER -->
			<section class="relative z-10 mb-10 pb-8 border-b border-slate-800/80">
				<div class="mb-6">
					<div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-cyan-400 mb-1">
						<span>💡</span>
						<span>·</span>
						<span class="lang-zh">底层原理与信息论机制</span>
						<span class="lang-en">Underlying Mechanics & Information Theory</span>
					</div>
					<h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold text-white tracking-tight">
						<span class="lang-zh">指纹追踪为何无孔不入？ · Why It Works</span>
						<span class="lang-en">Why It Works · The Mechanics of Uniqueness</span>
					</h2>
				</div>

				<div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
					<!-- Card 1: Akinator Analogy -->
					<div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 flex flex-col justify-between">
						<div>
							<div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 text-cyan-400 text-sm font-mono font-bold mb-3">
								<span class="p-1.5 rounded-lg bg-cyan-500/10 border border-cyan-500/30">🧞</span>
								<span class="lang-zh">1. 阿基纳托（Akinator）猜人比喻与比特</span>
								<span class="lang-en">1. The Akinator Analogy & Shannon Bits</span>
							</div>
							<h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">
								<span class="lang-zh">每一次提问，都将人群切掉一半</span>
								<span class="lang-en">Every Question Slices the Pool in Half</span>
							</h3>
							<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-3">
								<span class="lang-zh">
									你或许玩过“二十个问题”猜谜游戏或著名的阿基纳托（Akinator）精灵：系统先问“是女性吗？”直接淘汰 50% 的人；再问“活跃在科技界吗？”又淘汰 90%；紧接着问“在加州工作吗？”……经过 20 道看似普通的选择题，系统总能在全球名人群中准确说出你的心思。
								</span>
								<span class="lang-en">
									You may have played "Twenty Questions" or the popular Akinator web genie: the game asks "Is this person real?", immediately eliminating 50% of candidates; then "Are they active in technology?", shaving off another 90%; followed by "Do they live in California?"... Within 20 ordinary questions, the algorithm unerringly names your character out of billions.
								</span>
							</p>
							<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
								<span class="lang-zh">
									在香农信息论中，1 比特（bit）信息量意味着候选池被二等分（减小为原本的 1/2）。33 比特的正交信息能够产生 2³³ ≈ 85.8 亿种完全不重复的排列组合。浏览器指纹本质上就是由脚本主动向你的底层设备发起的二十道技术问答。
								</span>
								<span class="lang-en">
									In Shannon information theory, one bit of entropy halves the candidate pool. Exactly 33 orthogonal bits produce 2³³ ≈ 8.58 billion unique combinations—surpassing the entire human population. Browser fingerprinting is simply automated 20 Questions executed by script against your hardware.
								</span>
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-slate-800 text-[11px] font-mono text-cyan-400">
							<span class="lang-zh">信息论公式：熵 $H = \log_2(N)$ · 33 比特足以覆盖全人类</span>
							<span class="lang-en">Information formula: $H = \log_2(N)$ · 33 bits covers all humans</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Card 2: Network vs Code Executed -->
					<div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 flex flex-col justify-between">
						<div>
							<div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 text-indigo-400 text-sm font-mono font-bold mb-3">
								<span class="p-1.5 rounded-lg bg-indigo-500/10 border border-indigo-500/30">⚡</span>
								<span class="lang-zh">2. 网络层信号 vs 客户端代码执行层</span>
								<span class="lang-en">2. Network Signals vs Code Execution</span>
							</div>
							<h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">
								<span class="lang-zh">从被动报文转向主动硬件质询</span>
								<span class="lang-en">From Passive Packets to Active Hardware Interrogation</span>
							</h3>
							<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-3">
								<span class="lang-zh">
									传统的追踪依赖 IP 地址与 HTTP 请求头（如 User-Agent）。但 IP 地址是极度脆弱的：当你从家庭 Wi-Fi 切换到蜂窝 5G，或者开启 VPN 时，IP 会立即改变；同时现代浏览器对 User-Agent 进行了冻结（统一化）。
								</span>
								<span class="lang-en">
									Traditional tracking relied on IP addresses and HTTP request headers like User-Agent. But IP addresses are fragile: they shift whenever you transition from home Wi-Fi to cellular 5G, or activate a commercial VPN. Browser vendors have also frozen and standardized modern User-Agent strings.
								</span>
							</p>
							<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
								<span class="lang-zh">
									而代码执行层完全不同：追踪脚本不再“询问你叫什么”，而是命令浏览器：“在离屏画布上绘制一段带有次像素抗锯齿的复杂文字与渐变，并将像素缓冲区逐字节交还给我”。这直接测量了显卡驱动、光栅化管线与物理声卡的浮点实现——没有任何系统弹窗，无需任何用户授权。
								</span>
								<span class="lang-en">
									Code execution operates on an entirely different level: rather than asking who you are, the script commands: "Draw this complex antialiased text on an offscreen canvas and return the raw byte buffer." This directly measures your GPU driver, rasterizer pipeline, and audio DAC floating-point math—without a single permission dialog.
								</span>
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-slate-800 text-[11px] font-mono text-indigo-400">
							<span class="lang-zh">越过网络代理：VPN 改变 IP，却完全无法撼动 GPU 渲染特征</span>
							<span class="lang-en">VPN masks network IP, but leaves GPU rendering byte-for-byte identical</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Card 3: 1 in 2048 Worked Example -->
					<div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 flex flex-col justify-between">
						<div>
							<div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 text-emerald-400 text-sm font-mono font-bold mb-3">
								<span class="p-1.5 rounded-lg bg-emerald-500/10 border border-emerald-500/30">🧮</span>
								<span class="lang-zh">3. “1/2048”算例与条件独立性</span>
								<span class="lang-en">3. The "1 in 2,048" Example & Independence</span>
							</div>
							<h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">
								<span class="lang-zh">三个平凡特征如何构成罕见组合</span>
								<span class="lang-en">How Three Mundane Signals Make a Unique Match</span>
							</h3>
							<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-3">
								<span class="lang-zh">
									设想一个简单的数学推演：假定你的屏幕分辨率在互联网用户中占据 1/8（贡献 3 比特）；你的时区与地域属于 1/16 的人群（贡献 4 比特）；你的显卡型号与音频压缩器频响落在 1/16 的分支中（贡献 4 比特）。
								</span>
								<span class="lang-en">
									Consider a concrete mathematical scenario: suppose your display resolution places you in 1 out of 8 users (3 bits); your timezone locates you in 1 out of 16 (4 bits); and your GPU model with audio compressor frequency curve fits 1 in 16 (4 bits).
								</span>
							</p>
							<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
								<span class="lang-zh">
									若这三者彼此正交，三项乘积即可得出：$1 / (8 \times 16 \times 16) = 1 / 2048$（总计 $3 + 4 + 4 = 11$ 比特）。只需三个粗粒度的指标，你在两千余人构成的会议室中就已经是绝对独一无二的。当维度扩展到 15 个以上时，总乘积便会迅速跨越数十亿级别。
								</span>
								<span class="lang-en">
									If these three were orthogonal, the joint probability collapses to $1 / (8 \times 16 \times 16) = 1 / 2,048$ (totaling $3 + 4 + 4 = 11$ bits). With just three coarse observations, you are singular in an auditorium of two thousand. Expand this to 15 dimensions, and the product leaps into the billions.
								</span>
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="mt-4 pt-3 border-t border-slate-800 text-[11px] font-mono text-emerald-400">
							<span class="lang-zh">联合概率相乘：小概率事件在多维空间中指数级收敛</span>
							<span class="lang-en">Joint probability multiplication: exponential convergence</span>
						</div>
					</div>

					<!-- Card 4: Defenses and Paradox -->
					<div class="p-6 rounded-2xl bg-slate-900/70 border border-slate-800 flex flex-col justify-between">
						<div>
							<div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 text-amber-400 text-sm font-mono font-bold mb-3">
								<span class="p-1.5 rounded-lg bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/30">🛡️</span>
								<span class="lang-zh">4. 防御路线图与“特立独行者的悖论”</span>
								<span class="lang-en">4. Defenses & The Special Snowflake Paradox</span>
							</div>
							<h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-2">
								<span class="lang-zh">极致伪装有时反而成为最闪亮的灯塔</span>
								<span class="lang-en">Extreme Customization Acts as a Blinding Beacon</span>
							</h3>
							<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed mb-3">
								<span class="lang-zh">
									业界对抗指纹有两种主流哲学：<strong>同质化（Tor / Mullvad）</strong>通过隐藏所有个性化特征、固定窗口大小（Letterboxing）让所有用户汇入统一的“斑马群”；<strong>动态加噪（Brave Farbling）</strong>则在 Canvas 与音频渲染中注入每次会话微小变化的微量伪随机噪声，使得追踪器无法关联两次访问。
								</span>
								<span class="lang-en">
									Two philosophies dominate modern fingerprint defense: <strong>Uniformity (Tor / Mullvad)</strong> strips personalization and standardizes window sizing (letterboxing) to blend users into an identical herd; <strong>Farbling / Noise Injection (Brave)</strong> introduces tiny pseudo-random perturbations to canvas and audio outputs so hashes differ between domains and sessions.
								</span>
							</p>
							<p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
								<span class="lang-zh">
									然而，普通用户安装的“防指纹”浏览器扩展往往陷入<strong>特立独行者的悖论</strong>：如果全网只有 0.001% 的人安装了某款冷门修改 User-Agent 或阻断 Canvas 的插件，这个“阻断”行为本身就构成了一个极其罕见的 16 比特指纹！过度个性化的防御反而彻底坐实了你的唯一性。
								</span>
								<span class="lang-en">
									Yet popular third-party "anti-fingerprinting" extensions often trigger <strong>the special snowflake trap</strong>: if only 0.001% of web traffic carries an extension that blocks canvas reads with a canned error, that anomaly itself constitutes a blazing 16-bit fingerprint. Trying too hard to customize makes you unmistakably one of one.
								</span>
							</p>
